+    - Screen (`satchel.rs`): `Frame::new(sat, inv, gw, w, h)` is every rect in px (fractions of the height, text unit `craft::panel(0, w, h).2`), `Frame::hit` says what a finger is on (`Pick`), `draw` / `draw_pin` paint it; `lib.rs` only opens it (`open_satchel`: the inventory button, or a workbench with the book already open), routes the finger (`on_sat_tap`, `sat_pick`, a drag on the list scrolls, a press on the result held `HOLD_SECS` crafts all) and closes it (`close_screen` puts the grid and the held stack back in the bag first). `TouchUi::pack_open` is set while it is up (every press a tap, the four HUD buttons hidden), buttons: Sort, Shift, One above the bag, X at the corner; the book is not a button but a thing on the screen (below). The bag rises in 0.25 s, the book opens in 0.3 s (the cover narrows to its left edge, the hinge, and is gone at half way; both pages grow from the spine), a category slides in in 0.2 s. The world behind is dimmed.
+    - One layout (a first version had the cloth's four zones when closed; they sat mostly empty and the jump to the grid read badly): the bag is 9 x 3 + the belt + the armor row in 45% of the width (cells at least 8% of the height, checked by a test). The bag never moves (`opening_the_book_leaves_the_bag_alone`); the recipe book lies closed on its right from the first frame (`a_closed_book_lies_beside_the_bag_and_a_tap_opens_it`): a one page wide leather cover (`leather`, the bag's grain and stitches in red-brown) with a page edge, a strap and a gold clasp, the book icon (item 340), `Recipes` and `Tap to open`; a tap on it opens it, a `Close` tab above the spine (shown while open) shuts it, which puts the grid back in the bag as the old button did; a workbench opens the screen with the book already opening; every slot keeps its `SlotId` and always has its cell, so a held stack is put down by tapping a slot. Look, all drawn with quads (no texture): leather with a little grain, a seam of stitches and four rivets, a darker pocket band with a lit lip behind each row, a strap and buckle on the belt, and a slot rim tinted by `pack::category` (tools blue, food green, materials brown, other grey; the selected belt slot stays yellow). `pack::layout` / `ZONES` are no longer read by the satchel (the cloth still uses them).
     - Recipes (`world/book.rs`): `entries()` is every `craft::recipes()` entry (new accessors `Recipe::out` / `shape` / `pattern`, `craft::code` / `unpack` / `smelting` public) plus every smelting, in six `Cat`s; `craftable` / `missing` / `have` count the bag (main slots, the belt) and the grid; `fill` (a tap on a recipe) empties the grid into the bag, then takes one set of ingredients (main slots first, the belt last) into the recipe's own cells, and changes nothing when it fails (a 3x3 recipe at the 2x2 grid, something short, no room); `craft_all` is fill + `shift_click(Result)` in a loop until the bag runs dry or full; wool and dye match by colour (`craft::code`).
     - Notes (`book::Notes`, `<world>/book`, 69 bytes `BK1` + pin + 64 bytes of seen item ids, written with the level): `observe` marks every id the bag or grid holds each frame; `known(entry)` = its result or any ingredient was held; with `bookDiscovery:true` (the toggle on the right page) an unknown recipe is a dark `?` box and `???`, is not filled, and its card says to find an item; off (the default) everything shows. Pin: one recipe's card (result, each ingredient with have / need, green / red) at the left of the play HUD (`draw_pin`).
     - New: `packCloth` and `bookDiscovery` in `options.txt` (`Settings::pack_cloth`, `book_discovery`, default off).
